From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:13:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: Farble samples written to an already farbled
 AudioBuffer

copyToChannel after getChannelData wrote unfarbled samples into the
live view script already had, so the view mixed scaled and unscaled
samples. Samples written to a channel that's already farbled are now
scaled too.

Playing a buffer acquires its content, and the next getChannelData
attaches a copy of it. That copy was taken from samples that were
already scaled, so the channel stays marked as farbled, and a test
checks that it isn't scaled a second time.

internals.setFingerprintingProtection() lets tests turn protection on
despite test mode. A text test covers canvas, audio,
hardwareConcurrency, deviceMemory, the Chrome User-Agent, and
navigator.webdriver.
---
 .../Rust/src/web_audio/audio_buffer.rs        |  14 +++
 .../LibWeb/Bindings/RustBindingsServices.cpp  |   2 +-
 Libraries/LibWeb/Internals/Internals.cpp      |   6 +
 Libraries/LibWeb/Internals/Internals.h        |   1 +
 Libraries/LibWeb/Internals/Internals.idl      |   1 +
 .../expected/Fingerprinting/protection.txt    |  15 +++
 .../Text/input/Fingerprinting/protection.html | 106 ++++++++++++++++++
 7 files changed, 144 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 Tests/LibWeb/Text/expected/Fingerprinting/protection.txt
 create mode 100644 Tests/LibWeb/Text/input/Fingerprinting/protection.html

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/Bindings/Rust/src/web_audio/audio_buffer.rs b/Libraries/LibWeb/Bindings/Rust/src/web_audio/audio_buffer.rs
index b342d7050ced5012923adc887886c61dbe59f2f4..f9039b4ad5cbe2efae958ee57848f9807aadbe42 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/Bindings/Rust/src/web_audio/audio_buffer.rs
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/Bindings/Rust/src/web_audio/audio_buffer.rs
@@ -520,6 +520,20 @@ impl AudioBuffer {
                     count * size_of::<f32>(),
                 );
             });
+
+            // Fingerprinting protection: a live getChannelData() view already saw farbled samples, so newly written
+            // samples are farbled too. Unfarbled channels stay clean until the next read.
+            if channel.farbled {
+                // SAFETY: The channel's storage holds the buffer's length in f32 samples, and count of them start at
+                // the buffer offset.
+                let samples = unsafe {
+                    ak::slice_from_raw_parts_mut(
+                        channel.data.data().cast::<f32>().wrapping_add(buffer_offset as usize),
+                        count,
+                    )
+                };
+                farble_samples(cx.realm(), samples);
+            }
         }
         Ok(())
     }
